<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Devabhuti</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 73 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Devabhuti was the last king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shunga-empire">Shunga dynasty</a> of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puranas">Puranas</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banabhatta">Bana</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harshacharita">Harshacharita</a> record that around 73 BCE he was killed at the instigation of his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmins">Brahmin</a> minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vasudeva-kanva">Vasudeva Kanva</a>, who seized the throne and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanva-dynasty">Kanva dynasty</a>. Later sources portray him as a pleasure-loving ruler.</p></div>
